Section 5: A Heartbreak
Let's look for this URL to see if it was delivered in any emails. Who sent the email?
Given:
Email
| where link has "https://healthylifestyle.com/share/New_Diet_Plan_For_My_Love.xlsx"
Answer: marcella_flores@gmail.com

What was the subject of that email?
Answer: [EXTERNAL] RE: Relax with these yoga poses, baby! 🧘‍♂️

How many emails did marcella_flores@gmail.com send?
Let's try:
Email
| where sender == "marcella_flores@gmail.com"
Answer: 13

How many total domains were in the links seen in that email?
Given:
Email
| where sender == "marcella_flores@gmail.com"
| extend domain = parse_url(link).Host
| distinct tostring(domain)
So this one is a bit different. In these queries, we can parse out pieces of information from the full cell's worth of information. We can also then return that information in a string format (so, text) to make it easier to read and understand. So this query will look for emails Marcella has sent, look at the domain of the URLs she has sent by parsing out the "host" portion, and then outputting that information as a string.
Answer: 3

